From 8a4694d2f74adeef448cdfc6d6884ae77b603c3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:39:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] lifecycle guard: read expansion heredoc delimiters
 as bash does
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bash reads a heredoc delimiter word through its expansions without
performing them: `cat <<$(echo E)` ends at a line reading `$(echo E)`,
and backticks, `$((…))` and `${x:-a b}` likewise, spaces and all.
`$'…'` and `$"…"` are quoting, so `<<$'\x45'` ends at `E`.

_parse_heredoc_operator stopped such a word at its first `(` or space
(and kept the `$` of `$'E'`), so the body never found its terminator.
heredoc_body_spans stopped there, heredoc_scripts left the body in the
main walk, and a `}` line in it closed the outer `{` group early:
`{` / `cat <<$(echo E)` / `}` / `$(echo E)` / `cat f.py` / `} | python3`
scanned (False, None) although bash feeds f.py to python3.

Fix (option "parse as a literal word", not fail-closed):
tools/shell_heredoc_words.delimiter_expansion takes a `$(…)`, `$((…))`,
`${…}`, backtick or `$'…'` part whole (quote-aware, one line), decoding
ANSI-C escapes; `$"` drops the `$`. An expansion that does not close on
its line stays unparsed, as before.

Residual, not matched: bash reprints a `$(…)` delimiter from its parse,
so one holding a newline, a comment or a `case` gets a terminator text
this parser does not predict.

Five whys: the guard lost the feed because the group closed early ->
the body's `}` was walked as a command -> the body had no terminator ->
the delimiter parser cut the word at `(` -> it modelled delimiters as
plain/quoted characters only, with no expansion parts.

Proof: tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_heredoc_delimiters.py, 32 tests;
31 red on 62200e89a7, all green here, each shape also checked against
real bash with a harmless marker. Lifecycle guard suite
(tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard*.py): 28 files, 2047 passed.

Follow-up from review
https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/2942#pullrequestreview-5901857763
(card t_9da055deabdd8a23).
